FIX ROUND 430s5a2 for issue #430, SLICE 5a (decision 0104): THE HOST FLOOR, RE-VERIFIED AND REVIEWED WITH F2 CARRIED. The first run built the floor and fixed four of its review's five findings, then returned oversized on the fifth (F2), which needs files this unit may not edit. The controller has ruled F2 carried to a later unit. This round makes round 1's work one reviewed commit.

The branch is story-430-s5a-host-floor, checked out in this worktree off origin/main at 7ab429a9f. Round 1's two commits, 680f929c3 and 0e7dc81aa (kept at refs/keep/430s5a-r1), are already applied in the index, uncommitted. When you are done, the branch is 7ab429a9f plus ONE commit holding all of it. Do not rebase or merge main.

WHERE IT STANDS:
- **Round 1** (implement-issue-430-slice-5a-dec-c04d9e00) built everything in 5a's commission:
  - `forge.host/v3` with `timeout_floor_seconds` (1 to 7200, shared-local routes only), its refusals, and v1, v2 and v3 readers;
  - the attempt's deadline at dispatch.rs read through `self.cooldown.host` (`engine/dispatch/deadline.rs`), and the single attempt's words;
  - doctor's floor and egress-mismatch lines;
  - the minted contract with its lifecycle row, README entry and frozen digest.
  Its review (residual high, no security) found five things. The second implement visit (0e7dc81aa) fixed four, each with a removal control:
  - **F1, high:** the body runs on what provisioning left of the deadline, kept apart from the effective `Deadline` (`deadline_tests::the_driver_runs_on_what_provisioning_left_of_the_attempts_deadline`);
  - **F3:** an unreadable or invalid host names its file and cause in a normally failing, indeterminate or unspawned single attempt's words;
  - **F4:** a v1 or v2 floor refusal names its provider and route;
  - **F5:** a negative overflow refuses below the 1-second minimum.
- **F2** (a panel's or sequence's terminal words naming a raised deadline, and the panel and sequence half of F3) needs engine/panel.rs and engine/sequence.rs. 5a may not edit them: #430's 4c2a and 4c2b own them.
- The review also noted (INFO) that the missing-provider and missing-route lookups and short pins have no dedicated coverage cases.

THE CONTROLLER'S RULING (the-forge-9d, under the operator's standing ruling of 2026-11-04; recorded on #430 c-6729740847): **F2, with F3's panel and sequence half, is carried to a follow-up unit, 5a2, queued after 4c2a and 4c2b land.** Panels and sequences already run under the raised deadline; only their words wait. **For this round's review, F2 is ruled and is not a finding.** It is named as an ASK. Every other requirement of 5a's commission stands.

WHAT TO DO:
0. Read 5a's commission requirements, restated in GATES and CONTENTION below, and decision 0104 rulings 1 to 4.
1. **Re-verify round 1's fixes.** Run each removal control (i) to (vii) from round 1 again, and record each observed failure and restore in the commit message:
   - (i) a cloud link after a shared-local one;
   - (ii) a longer authored limit;
   - (iii) the highest floor of a panel's launched members;
   - (iv) run_body handed the whole bound;
   - (v) an unreadable host named only on a deadline kill;
   - (vi) a v1 or v2 refusal without provider and route;
   - (vii) a negative overflow above the maximum.
2. **Close the coverage INFO:** add tests for a floor lookup whose provider is absent from the host file, one whose route is absent, and a short or empty pin, each reading as no floor and keeping the seat's limit.
3. **Fold** round 1's two commits and this round's change into one commit. Keep round 1's first subject and tell all of it in the body, with F2 named as carried by the controller's ruling.
4. **Do not edit** engine/panel.rs, engine/sequence.rs, engine/cooldown.rs or engine.rs.

ASKS TO NAME (for the PR):
- **F2 carried** to 5a2, after 4c2a and 4c2b: the panel and sequence words for a raised deadline and an unreadable host;
- the floor's cap of 7200, pinned to the fleet's staleness bound by `the_floor_cap_is_the_fleets_attempt_bound`;
- a sequence's floor taken attempt-wide, with per-step floors left to a later unit;
- an unreadable or invalid host file keeps the seat's limit and names itself, rather than parking;
- the minted `forge.host/v3`, its reader of v1, v2 and v3, and v1's and v2's unchanged bytes;
- the public API additions (`admission::{declared_routes, HostRoutes, RouteDecl}`), exactly as regenerated, and any new ask.

GATES:
- cargo fmt --all -- --check
- cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings
- cargo test -p brokkr-runtime --lib --locked -- admission:: engine::dispatch (timeout 280; split by module if it cannot finish)
- cargo test -p brokkr-runtime --test it --locked -- frozen_contracts:: (timeout 280)
- cargo test -p brokkr-cli --lib --locked -- doctor:: (timeout 280)
- cargo test -p brokkr-cli --test it --locked -- contract_lifecycle:: doc_truth:: doc_samples:: (timeout 280)
- typos --hidden; quality/ratchet.sh files, clones and api; git diff --check
- TMPDIR stays OUTSIDE this worktree (use /var/tmp, created in the same command if missing). Before reporting, `git status --short` shows no untracked file.
- Run every command in the foreground and wait for it. Never end your turn with a background job pending: this seat is non-interactive.
- A seat whose commands run through the `workspace` tool has a 300-second response limit per call. A call that outlasts it leaves its command running and blocks the calls behind it, including the write of your result file. So:
  - wrap every command in `timeout 280` there;
  - if a gate still cannot finish inside the limit, report it UNVERIFIED rather than retrying it;
  - write your result file before any optional extra check.
- Every new line is covered by a test. Exact coverage counts lines, branches and functions: an if-let's miss is a branch, a closure is a function, and a line holding only a `?` is its error arm. No new function may pass CC 15 (`quality/ratchet.sh crap`), and each `?` counts one. No file may pass its ceiling (production 800, tests 2,000), and a file already past it may not grow.
- Commit ONCE, signed off (`git commit -s`): the branch is 7ab429a9f plus ONE commit holding round 1's two commits and this round's change, with round 1's first subject ("admission: a shared-local host floor raises an attempt's deadline (decision 0104 slice 5a, #430)") kept and the body telling all of it. Leave a blank line before the trailers. "Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>" comes LAST, directly after the sign-off. Record each removal control in the commit message. Never push.

ASKS TO NAME (for the PR):
- the floor's cap of 7200 and its tie to the fleet's staleness bound, and any test that pins the two together;
- a sequence's floor taken attempt-wide, and per-step floors left to a later unit;
- an unreadable host file keeps the seat's limit and names itself, rather than parking;
- the minted `forge.host/v3`, its reader of v1, v2 and v3, and v1's and v2's unchanged bytes;
- any public API growth, exactly as regenerated, and any new ask.

SIZE: about 250 to 400 production and 500 to 900 test lines at the first implement visit, and about twice that by merge. #430's slices 4a to 4c1 grew two to three times in review.

KNOWN FLAKES, not this branch's:
- capability_broker tests and `machine_proof::` runs failing "MCP server box filesystem identity is not protected" under host load;
- brokkr-runtime engine::broker admission tests ending `Identity(Expired)` under load;
- heap_costs' one-byte compare difference under load;
- brokkr-store's `concurrent_processes` child timing out in `Store::open` (`Contended { operation: "ensure_wal" }`) under load;
- brokkr-cli's lib binary hanging in a `broker::rpc` pipe deadlock (#1003).

If verify fails on one of these alone, the implement visit reruns it on the host alone (`-- --exact`, with HOME set), quotes both results, makes no commit, and reports COMPLETE, not blocked.

CONTENTION (NEVER message the-forge-9d, the-forge-20 or any brokkr-wt-* seat):
- **#430 slice 4c2a** (another lane, running) is in brokkr-runtime's engine/cooldown.rs and a new cooldown child, cooldown/probe.rs, engine/cursor.rs, engine/panel.rs, brokkr-core's payload/provider_wait.rs, decision 0103, and the public-API snapshots. **4c2b** follows it, in engine/sequence.rs.
- **#753 slice 4** (other lanes) is in brokkr-core's seat and summary modules, brokkr-store's event_index, seat_read, seat_summary and compare, and brokkr-view's analytics.
- **9d** owns the CI workflows, scripts/test-shards.sh and scripts/shard-runner.py.
- **This unit edits:**
  - brokkr-runtime's admission/host.rs (the field and the call) and a new host child, and host/tests.rs or a new host test file;
  - contracts/host.v3.schema.json, contracts/README.md, docs/guides/versioning.md, and brokkr-runtime/tests/frozen_contracts.rs;
  - engine/dispatch.rs (the deadline line and its call) and a new dispatch child;
  - brokkr-cli's doctor (a new child, or providers.rs);
  - the host file's guide;
  - the public-API snapshots, if anything public grows.
  - Leave everything else, engine/cooldown.rs, engine/sequence.rs, engine/panel.rs and engine.rs above all.

Every review position, panel member or chief, is READ-ONLY: it changes no tracked file and makes no commit. For a scratch, use `git worktree add` or `git archive HEAD | tar -x` into /var/tmp, never a byte copy of this worktree. It reports each finding as a test case: the host file planted (version, routes, classes and floors), the seat's limit, the chain or panel or sequence launched and the candidates it reached, and the deadline, words, doctor line or refusal observed against the ones expected.

Decisions: 0104 (accepted; rulings 1 to 4; slice 5a); 0068 rulings 5 and 6; 0036 (egress class, route predicate); 0082 (minting forge.host/v3); 0103 (the host seam, 4c1, as built); 0071 rulings 1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 8 and 9; 0063 (Linux and macOS).

YOUR SEAT: you run on dsh (DeepSeek Flash, DeepSeek's platform), unboxed with dsh's own tools, at the operator's word (2026-10-26). Sign off every commit (`git commit -s`).
